# Kino Corrects the Fallacy

---

Finally, Jesuit missionary Eusebio Kino challenged the idea that California was an island after he was sent to Baja California in 1681. Kino suspected that the blue abalone shells he received as gifts from indigenous peoples in Arizona must have come overland from the coast. Kino, who had been well-educated in Europe, made more than forty expeditions throughout the southwest. He confirmed his suspicions about California in 1701 after his surveys indicated that it was indeed a peninsula. 

